=== exp2: AG+GEMM overlap granularity sweep ===
world 4, GEMM on GPU 0, push mode, one comm stream per peer
GPU 0: NVIDIA H800  sm_90  132 SMs  1980 MHz
GPU 1: NVIDIA H800  sm_90  132 SMs  1980 MHz
GPU 2: NVIDIA H800  sm_90  132 SMs  1980 MHz
GPU 3: NVIDIA H800  sm_90  132 SMs  1980 MHz

--- 8192x8192x8192 fp16 (shard M=2048, AG volume 96.0 MiB): full GEMM 1688.7 us, 651.1 TFLOP/s ---
   S   rows  chunkMiB |  t_seg us  segeff |    t_comm    GB/s |  t_ovl us  TFLOPs  ovl_eff   bub% | ver
   1   2048     32.00 |    1692.1   0.998 |     576.4   174.6 |    1863.6   590.0    0.703  10.1% | -
   2   1024     16.00 |    1730.2   0.976 |     576.3   174.7 |    1743.8   630.5    0.976   0.8% | -
   4    512      8.00 |    1861.1   0.907 |     576.0   174.8 |    1875.0   586.4    0.976   0.7% | -
   8    256      4.00 |    3555.7   0.475 |     576.2   174.7 |    3592.2   306.1    0.937   1.0% | -
  16    128      2.00 |    7115.6   0.237 |     576.0   174.8 |    7177.9   153.2    0.892   0.9% | -
  32     64      1.00 |   14225.1   0.119 |     590.3   170.5 |   14346.2    76.6    0.795   0.9% | -

seg_eff = t_full/t_seg (segmentation-only GEMM efficiency).
ovl_eff = (t_seg + t_comm - t_ovl) / min(t_seg, t_comm); 1.0 means the
shorter phase is fully hidden. bub% = t_ovl over max(t_seg, t_comm).
The sweet spot is the S with the lowest t_ovl: finer chunks start compute
earlier but pay tile quantization + per-chunk signalling; coarser chunks
expose the first chunk's flight time.
